 "briefing": "# Canva Briefing: Changes from 16 October to 15 November 2026\n\n## Summary\n\nThis briefing could not confirm any verified changes at Canva in the 30-day window from 16 October to 15 November 2026. Every search attempt returned a rate-limit error, so no dated articles, press releases, filings, or other sources were retrieved. The absence of results is not evidence that nothing happened. Canva may have made news, launched products, named executives, or signed deals in this period, and the research cannot show whether it did.\n\nBefore the 17 November meeting, the four categories should be checked directly against the primary sources listed below.\n\n## Research Status\n\nThe research covered four categories: news, product launches, hires, and deals. Each category was searched with multiple query variations, and each search failed with the same error. The following were not accessed:\n\n- Canva's newsroom, blog, and press releases\n- Canva's developer resources\n- Reuters, Bloomberg, TechCrunch, The Information, the Financial Times, the Wall Street Journal, and the Australian Financial Review\n- SEC or ASX/ASIC filings, and counterparty press releases\n\nBecause no source was reached, no fact in this briefing is dated, cited to a publication, or confirmed. Nothing below should be read as a confirmed \"no change\" finding.\n\n## Status by Category\n\n### News\n\nNo verified news items were found for the window. Searches covering financial and user metrics, legal or regulatory matters, leadership statements, and IPO or valuation commentary did not return results. Canva's newsroom and the major business outlets were not successfully checked.\n\n### Product Launches\n\nNo verified product launches were found for the window. Searches covering new features, AI tools, platform or developer releases, and pricing or plan changes did not return results. The developer resources at canva.dev and the Canva blog remain unchecked and are the most likely places to confirm launches.\n\n### Hires and Departures\n\nNo verified executive hires, departures, promotions, board appointments, or notable moves were found for the window. Searches covering executive appointments and leadership changes did not return results. LinkedIn announcements and newsroom appointment notices were not checked.\n\n### Deals\n\nNo verified acquisitions, investments, funding rounds, partnerships, customer agreements, or channel agreements were found for the window. Searches across these deal types did not return results. Canva's newsroom and counterparty press releases were not checked.\n\n## Priority Checks Before the Meeting\n\nThe following sources should be reviewed in this order, with each item dated to the 16 October to 15 November window:\n\n1. Canva newsroom, for official press releases and announcements [1]\n2. Canva blog, for product and company updates [2]\n3. Canva developer site, for platform, API, and app-related releases [3]\n4. Business press coverage (Reuters, Bloomberg, TechCrunch, The Information, Australian Financial Review), searched for \"Canva\" with the date range set to the window\n5. Counterparty newsrooms, for any partner or acquisition announcements found in the above sources\n\nEach verified item should record its headline, publication date, and URL. Any item whose date or source cannot be confirmed should be flagged as uncertain.\n\n## Open Questions for the Meeting\n\n1. **What in the last 30 days should we treat as Canva's official record?** No announcements from the newsroom or blog could be verified for this window. Asking which releases were published, and which were not yet publicly covered, will show whether our picture of recent activity is complete.\n\n2. **What product changes have shipped recently, and what is scheduled next?** No launches or platform releases could be confirmed. Asking about recent feature, AI, pricing, and developer updates will clarify what has changed and what may affect our work.\n\n3. **Have there been any leadership changes or deal activity in the past month that affect our counterpart or the scope of this discussion?** No hires, departures, or agreements could be verified. Asking directly will identify who we should engage with and whether any agreements could affect the topics we plan to discuss.\n\n## Sources\n\n[1] Canva Newsroom (not accessed; listed as a primary source to check): https://www.canva.com/newsroom\n[2] Canva Blog (not accessed; listed as a primary source to check): https://www.canva.com/blog\n[3] Canva Developers (not accessed; listed as a primary source to check): https://www.canva.dev",
